  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>tr_predict_fraud - scores this week's new orders with the saved fraud model, says why, and writes the
scores to a CSV file and to MySQL.
Run by jb_fraud_main_job, after tr_train_model_fraud; needs h2o-env and the fraud database
(fraud_schema.sql).

1. csvi-customer, csvi-customer_billing, csvi-customer_transaction: CSV file input, this week's files:
   week_customer.csv, week_customer_billing.csv, week_transaction_details.csv.
2. slkp-customer, slkp-transaction_details: Stream lookup, one row per transaction.
3. map-features: Mapping, runs tr_features.ktr, the same features as training.
4. sv-convert_booleans_to_numbers: Select values, customer_id, transaction_id and the eight features.
5. py-predict_fraud: Python Executor, h2o-env's python.exe, All rows as test; loads
   train_model_output/gbm_fraud; the probability, the flag at 0.5, and top_reason from
   predict_contributions.
6. Predict Fraud: Text file output, output/credit_card_fraud_&lt;HHmmss&gt;.csv with a header.
7. iu-transaction_scores: Insert / Update, 4 copies, fraud.transaction_scores keyed on transaction_id.

Shipped data: this week's 10,000 scored, 38 flagged at 0.5; the first, transaction 200001, has
fraud_probability 0.0020 and top_reason total_transactions_to_date.</note>
      <xloc>224</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>598</width>
      <heigth>332</heigth>
